@{
    ViewData["Title"] = Lang.T("Wind & Missing Shingles Repair | Charlotte NC", "Reparación por viento y shingles faltantes | Charlotte NC");
}
<section class="problem-hero"><div class="site-shell problem-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Wind and missing shingle repair · Charlotte, NC</p><h1>Wind can break the roof seal before a shingle disappears.</h1><p>Lifted, creased, torn or displaced shingles can interrupt the water-shedding surface. Majestic inspects the visible pattern, surrounding attachment and repairability before recommending a repair or replacement.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Request free inspection →")</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="tel:+19808005991">@Lang.T("Call Majestic")</a></div></div><figure class="problem-hero-visual"><img src="/damage-guides/wind-damage-example.webp" alt="Educational example of lifted and missing asphalt shingles after wind"/><div class="problem-icon problem-icon-wind" aria-label="WIND"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational damage example · inspection determines the actual condition")</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="problem-urgent"><div class="site-shell"><strong>@Lang.T("SAFETY FIRST")</strong><p>Stay on the ground during high wind. Keep away from loose materials, power lines and falling limbs. Wait for safe weather before any roof access.</p></div></section><section class="problem-signs section"><div class="site-shell problem-clues-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What you may notice")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Visible clues help define the inspection—not the final diagnosis.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("Use these examples to describe what you see from a safe location. A photo cannot confirm every roof layer, hidden moisture, cause or repairability.")</p></div><figure class="problem-clue-photo"><img src="/damage-guides/wind-damage-example.webp" alt="Educational example of lifted and missing asphalt shingles after wind"/><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational reference—not a Majestic customer case.")</figcaption></figure><ul><li>Missing tabs or full shingles</li><li>Creases across lifted shingles</li><li>Raised edges that no longer lie flat</li><li>Exposed nails or underlayment</li><li>Damaged ridge caps, fascia or soffit</li></ul></div></section><section class="problem-first section" id="first-steps"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Before the crew arrives")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Five first steps for the homeowner.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Do only what can be completed safely from the ground or a stable interior area.")</p></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Photograph visible roof areas from the ground.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Save any fallen roofing material without altering it.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Check ceilings and attic only from safe accessible areas.</p></li><li><span>04</span><p>Record the storm date and when the condition was discovered.</p></li><li><span>05</span><p>Request inspection before the next hard rain when possible.</p></li></ol></div></section><section class="problem-process section"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading centered-heading"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("How Majestic handles this specific problem")</p><h2>@Lang.T("A documented path from concern to completed roof.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("The exact scope depends on safe access and what the inspection confirms. These five stages show how this particular roof condition is evaluated and repaired.")</p></div><div class="problem-process-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Pattern inspection</h3><p>We identify affected slopes, edges, ridges and nearby components.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Material assessment</h3><p>We review brittleness, seal condition, availability and whether adjacent shingles can be manipulated safely.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Temporary plan</h3><p>Exposed areas may receive temporary protection when safe and appropriate.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Repairability decision</h3><p>We explain whether isolated replacement can integrate with the existing system.</p></article><article><span>05</span><h3>Authorized work</h3><p>The agreed repair or replacement is completed and documented.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="arrival-section section" id="arrival"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What happens when we arrive")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Six checkpoints from arrival through closeout.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Majestic documents the roof as a construction system, explains choices before work begins and keeps insurance coverage decisions separate from contractor work.")</p></div><div class="arrival-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Arrival, interview and safety check</h3><p>The technician confirms what happened, when the condition was first noticed, whether water is entering now and which interior rooms are affected. Before using a ladder, Majestic checks weather, electrical, tree, structural and fall hazards and explains any access limitation.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Interior and ground-level reference</h3><p>When relevant and accessible, the team starts at the stain, drip or impacted room, reviews the attic from a safe access point and then walks the exterior perimeter. This creates a reference line between the interior evidence and the roof area above it.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Roof-system inspection</h3><p>When safe access is available, Majestic reviews affected slopes plus shingles, ridge and hip caps, valleys, flashing, pipe boots, vents, skylights, roof edges, gutters, fascia and soffit. Wide photographs show location; detail photographs show the condition.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Measurements and factual documentation</h3><p>The record identifies visible conditions, roof geometry, affected components and estimated quantities. Storm-related observations are separated from age, maintenance, installation details and hidden conditions that cannot be confirmed without authorized removal.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h3>Options explained before authorization</h3><p>Majestic explains immediate protection, localized repair, section rebuild and replacement paths when applicable. The homeowner receives a written roofing path and can choose an out-of-pocket project or use the factual documents in a claim they manage with their carrier.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h3>Construction, verification and closeout</h3><p>After a written scope is approved, materials and schedule are confirmed. Majestic performs the authorized roofing work, controls debris and cleanup, photographs completion and provides the applicable invoice, warranty and project-closeout documents.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-repairs section" id="repairs"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Repair options")</p><h2>@Lang.T("The inspection determines which option can be built reliably.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Final materials, quantities, code requirements and hidden conditions are confirmed in the written scope.")</p></div><div class="problem-repair-grid"><article><h3>Individual shingle replacement</h3><p>Remove and replace isolated damaged shingles when compatible material and a safe installation path exist.</p></article><article><h3>Ridge or edge repair</h3><p>Replace damaged caps, starter or edge components and inspect adjacent fastening.</p></article><article><h3>Slope repair</h3><p>A larger roof plane may require work when damage or material condition extends beyond isolated shingles.</p></article><article><h3>Full replacement</h3><p>May be appropriate for widespread wind effects, brittle systems, repeated failures or unavailable matching materials.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-source"><div class="site-shell"><span>i</span><p>Roof performance depends on the complete system, including locked edges, attachment and sealed decking—not only the visible shingle. <a href="https://ibhs.org/roof-101/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the source ↗</a></p></div></section><section class="faq-section section"><div class="site-shell faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("FAQ")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Clear expectations before work begins.")</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>@Lang.T("Is the inspection free?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic provides a free roof inspection, photographs, a report, estimated measurements and a written project path, subject to safe access.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Does the inspection guarantee insurance coverage?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("No. Majestic documents roofing conditions and scope. The carrier independently decides coverage and payment.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Can I pay out of pocket?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic can explain an out-of-pocket repair or replacement path as well as the construction documentation used for a claim-related project.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("How far do you travel?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Roof inspections are available approximately 90 minutes from Charlotte or Rock Hill, subject to address and schedule confirmation. Raleigh is not in the service area.")</p></details></div></div></section><section class="resource-cta section"><div class="site-shell"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Free inspection")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Photos, report, estimated measurements and a written project path.")</h2><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Start my request →")</a></div></section>
